{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017936-spirit-sphere-against-demons","id":1017936,"title":"Spirit sphere against demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-15T21:00:16-08:00","id":1017936,"title":"Spirit sphere against demons","content":"As far as I understand, spirit 4 is when Spirit sphere can be employed against the fallen. Therefore, what exactly (other than exorcisms) can be done? Once they're exorcised are they banished to the umbra or do they just vanish? Is there a specific rote to binding/exorcising demons? Imprisoning them in human bodies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:08:38-08:00","id":1017937,"title":"","content":"What makes you think demons can only be affected by Spirit 4? Because that's not written anywhere in the books, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 is needed for exorcism, yes, but that applies to any spirit entity that can possess people (or objects or places, for that matter). That's just an inherent part of that level of the Sphere. You use the same rank to force spirit entities into objects - or indeed to <i>force</i> them to do anything.<br /> <br /> The fallen are spirits, just like any other. The word &quot;demon&quot; itself is vague at best, and could be (and has been) used to describe any number of Umbrood. The Book of Madness has a section on Infernalism, and lists a number of beings that are not Fallen Angels that one can engage soul trade with (like Ares, Greek god of war).<br /> <br /> As such, Spirit treats them the same way you'd treat any Umbrood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:22:46-08:00","id":1017940,"title":"","content":"That depends on a lot of things, and it seems you don't know Demon's rules. So, crash course.<br /> <br /> 1- The Fallen can be exorcised, bound or warded with common human faith, not even True Faith is necessary.<br /> <br /> 2- Bound or warded off, a Demon remains in the host.<br /> <br /> 3- If banished somehow from the host, the Demon either gets little time to find another, or is sent to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> 4- As a rule of thumb, only a Summon Ritual can reliably get a Fallen out of Hell. It can be performed by a common human, though.<br /> <br /> On crossover rules, that's a tricky question, and depends on what your ST wants out of the Fallen.<br /> <br /> - If Fallen are like any other spirit, so you can do to them what you can to any other spirit, they just have very specialized charms to make it for how they function.<br /> - If Fallen are protected by the host, maybe Matter or Life, depending on the kind of Host, have to be added.<br /> - If the ST allows it, Mind can be used on a living host to create and affect a second mind that can fight with the demon for control of the host.<br /> - If the ST buys heavily on the Fallen Angels from Creation thing, Prime can be necessary, and new limits can be set, but at ST discretion.<br /> <br /> Now, if the ST isn't actually using Fallen from Demon, but another kind of spirit, so most they are ultimately spirits, as malleable by default as any other. There are several distinct rules for demons in the setting, so it isn't simple to precise answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:39:55-08:00","id":1017971,"title":"","content":"By demons I'm referring to demons others can play, not familiars or whatnot you can summon from the Umbra. Typically host-bound demons. How do I utilize spirit against them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T00:03:46-08:00","id":1017988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017936-spirit-sphere-against-demons?p=1017971#post1017971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By demons I'm referring to demons others can play, not familiars or whatnot you can summon from the Umbra. Typically host-bound demons. How do I utilize spirit against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you use Spirit the same as with other spirits. If they don't consist of physical matter (and aren't Chimerical, like from Changeling; possibly even then), they are ephemeral beings, and thus you use Spirit. Whether it's a spirit that is patterned after human belief of demons, or a capital-d Demon from Actual Hell, is immaterial in this case, because the spirit in question in immaterial.<br /> <br /> You use Spirit 1 to sense them, Spirit 2 to speak to and summon them, Spirit 3 to harm them, Spirit 4 to exorcise or contain them, and Spirit 5 to annihilate them completely. If the demon is bound to a host, you might need to add Life 2/3 to these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-16-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T04:31:51-08:00","id":1018022,"title":"","content":"My answer was all about the demons meant for PCs.<br /> <br /> Spirit will work just fine as with any other spirit, unless your ST don't want to.<br /> <br /> What is fair, since they are meant as snow-flake spirits, but isn't required, specially if no PC is one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}